content.text:
Use the `@variant` directive with the breakpoint name inside your custom CSS. This example is mine, built from the syntax in the docs (the docs only show `dark` and `hover`):

```css
:root {
  --my-var: 1rem;

  @variant md {
    --my-var: 2rem;
  }
}
```

`@variant` takes any Tailwind variant, including breakpoint variants like `md`. You can stack variants (`@variant md:hover`) or comma-separate them (`@variant hover, focus`).

Source: `src/docs/adding-custom-styles.mdx`, "Using custom CSS → Using variants" (lines 299–400). I didn't find a breakpoint-specific example there, so `@variant md` is inferred from the general syntax.

For custom breakpoints, see `src/docs/responsive-design.mdx`, "Using custom breakpoints → Customizing your theme". It defines them with `--breakpoint-*` theme variables.

